    description: "Cornus alba ‘Elegantissima’ combines cream-edged grey-green leaves with vivid red young stems, so its strongest season begins after the foliage falls. Moved from Back Bed 2 to the front wall bed in July 2026, it now needs establishment water before any ambitious stooling. Once rooted, removing a proportion of old dull stems each spring will keep the winter framework colourful without forcing a recently moved plant to rebuild everything at once.",
    months: ["May", "Jun"], size: "2–3m", sizeDetail: "Suckering shrub of comparable spread if uncontained", position: "Sun or partial shade", positionDetail: "Good light strengthens variegation and stem colour", soil: "Moist but well-drained", soilDetail: "Tolerates clay and seasonal moisture", hardiness: "H6", hardinessDetail: "Fully hardy", feature: "Cream-edged leaves and red winter stems", featureDetail: "Young stems carry the brightest colour", identity: "Cornus alba ‘Elegantissima’", identityDetail: "Cultivar confirmed",
