    problem: { name: "Reversion", sign: "Strong shoots carry plain green leaves without the cream margin", response: "Trace reverted shoots to their origin and remove them completely before they dominate the variegated plant." },
    about: "Cornus alba is an Asian dogwood grown for coloured winter stems. ‘Elegantissima’ adds a broad cream margin to the leaves and forms a vigorous suckering shrub. Annual total coppicing gives maximum stem colour but removes scale and spring flowers; selective renewal is a better fit while Oak Lodge wants both structure and red young wood.", provenance: "Cultivar identity is confirmed by the established record and diagnostic cream variegation with red stems.", family: "Cornaceae", genus: "Cornus", foliage: "Deciduous and cream-variegated", habit: "Bushy, suckering and upright", role: "Variegated summer mass and red winter framework below the window", observation: "Relocation gives this vigorous shrub more room and moves its red stems into the front winter view.", added: "Moved from Back Bed 2 in July 2026", status: "Prioritise re-establishment through 2026–27; delay strong renewal pruning until vigorous new growth proves the move succeeded.", source: RHS.cornus,
