    description: "This Kniphofia lifts dense orange-red poker spikes above a fountain of narrow strap leaves at the front of the wall bed. Individual tubular flowers open progressively along each spike, creating a long nectar source for bees. The move from Back Bed 1 gives it a sunnier open position, but cultivar-level care remains impossible until mature height, the yellow-to-red colour transition and flowering time are recorded.",
    months: ["Jul", "Aug", "Sep"], size: "90–150cm", sizeDetail: "Cultivar-dependent flower height; clump 60–90cm wide", position: "Full sun", positionDetail: "Open light is essential for strong flowering", soil: "Fertile and well-drained", soilDetail: "Moist in growth, never waterlogged in winter", hardiness: "Around H5", hardinessDetail: "Most garden hybrids are hardy with drainage", feature: "Orange-red torch flowers", featureDetail: "Tubular florets open progressively along upright spikes", identity: "Kniphofia garden hybrid", identityDetail: "Genus secure; cultivar not recorded",
