    caution: "Leucothoe is harmful if eaten. Wear gloves for prolonged handling and keep clippings away from pets and children.", about: "Leucothoe are evergreen members of the heath family with leathery leaves and spring clusters of small urn-shaped flowers. ‘Little Flames’ is a compact cultivar selected for bright red new growth and a size suitable for small beds and containers. Its H7 rating contrasts with the tender foliage shrubs elsewhere in the front garden.", provenance: "The retained name and diagnostic red young growth match the RHS cultivar record.", family: "Ericaceae", genus: "Leucothoe", foliage: "Evergreen; red when young", habit: "Compact and bushy", role: "Low red-flushed evergreen beneath the trellis", observation: "The new growth repeats the Dogwood’s winter red at a much smaller scale.", added: "Added July 2026", status: "Monitor soil reaction and avoid allowing lime-rich rubble at the wall base to raise pH around the roots.", source: RHS.leucothoe,
