    under: "new leaves wilting and scorching during a prolonged wall-side drought", over: "purple-brown spotting and heavy leaf drop after cold wet conditions", spring: "Photograph the new flush and flowers, then make only light shaping cuts after the first colour display.", summer: "Water only through sustained drought and keep the new underplanting from competing directly at the stem bases.", autumn: "Leave sound growth to mature and clear diseased fallen foliage from beneath the canopy.", winter: "Avoid stimulating soft growth and inspect the branch framework for crossing stems or wall contact.",
