    about: "Physocarpus opulifolius is a North American suckering shrub named for its bladder-like fruits and peeling mature bark. Little Devil is a compact selection, accepted by the RHS and also associated with the name ‘Donna May’. Its dark leaves colour best in good light, while the shrub remains fully hardy and adaptable.", provenance: "The retained Little Devil label and dark compact growth match the accepted RHS record.", family: "Rosaceae", genus: "Physocarpus", foliage: "Deciduous; burgundy-purple", habit: "Compact, bushy and lightly suckering", botanicalLabel: "Accepted name", botanicalValue: "Little Devil; synonym ‘Donna May’", role: "Dark compact foliage under the window", observation: "The first plant repeats the wine tones of Lady in Red at a smaller scale.", added: "Added during the June 2026 Front Bed 4 replant", status: "Let the shrub establish its natural outline before deciding whether any renewal pruning is necessary.", source: RHS.littleDevil,
