    about: "Lady in Red is the trade name for Physocarpus opulifolius ‘Tuilad’, a compact-to-medium ninebark selected for fresh red leaves, later bronze, and pink summer flowers. It shares the species’ hardiness and layered bark but stays substantially smaller than an unrestricted seedling form.", provenance: "The retained label and foliage match the RHS trade-name record.", family: "Rosaceae", genus: "Physocarpus", foliage: "Deciduous; red becoming bronze", habit: "Bushy and suckering", botanicalLabel: "Name status", botanicalValue: "Trade name for ‘Tuilad’", role: "Taller dark foliage behind the centre-left planting", observation: "This specimen creates a red-bronze middle layer between the climbing rose and front-edge plants.", added: "Added during the June 2026 Front Bed 4 replant", status: "Keep the outline natural and compare its mature height with the second Lady in Red.", source: RHS.ladyRed,
