    description: "Purple Gem (‘Purplerij1’) occupies the ivy corner, where glossy evergreen leaves and purple-tinted young stems provide quiet structure through deep shade. Its tiny cream flowers are visually modest but release strong fragrance in winter, followed by dark berries where pollination succeeds. The main management task is not elaborate pruning: it is keeping ivy and larger roots from smothering a low, slowly expanding shrub.",
