    description: "Pieris japonica ‘Flaming Silver’ combines three foliage stages in one compact shrub: new growth opens bright red, matures green and retains a bold silvery-white margin. Branching clusters of creamy bell flowers appear in spring. This display depends on acidic soil and healthy fine roots; lime-rich rubble near the wall or repeated tap-water alkalinity can cause chlorosis long before the plant is visibly dry.",
    months: ["Mar", "Apr", "May"], size: "1–1.5m", sizeDetail: "Erect shrub spreading about 50–100cm", position: "Sun or partial shade", positionDetail: "Shelter red young growth from harsh frost", soil: "Acidic and humus-rich", soilDetail: "Moist but well-drained; use ericaceous mulch", hardiness: "H5", hardinessDetail: "Hardy; young growth benefits from shelter", feature: "Red flush becoming silver-edged green", featureDetail: "Cream bell flowers in spring", identity: "Pieris japonica ‘Flaming Silver’", identityDetail: "Cultivar confirmed",
