    problem: { name: "Centre dieback", sign: "A brown hollow develops in the middle of an otherwise living tuft", response: "Lift and divide in spring, replanting compact blue outer pieces into lean free-draining soil." },
    about: "Festuca glauca is an evergreen European fescue selected in gardens for blue foliage. ‘Elijah Blue’ forms especially intense ice-blue cushions and remains compact, though clumps commonly lose vigour in the centre after several years. Division preserves the named cultivar and restores a dense juvenile outline.", provenance: "The three-plant label and diagnostic ice-blue compact habit support ‘Elijah Blue’.", family: "Poaceae", genus: "Festuca", foliage: "Evergreen and ice-blue", habit: "Densely tufted", role: "Three repeated blue-grey cushions along the front edge", observation: "The fine cool foliage separates the larger gold, red and green shrub leaves behind.", added: "Added during the June 2026 Front Bed 4 replant", status: "Keep soil lean and compare the three tufts for drainage-related differences.", source: RHS.festuca,
