    description: "The Astrantia trio combines ‘Buckland’, ‘Claret’ and ‘Star of Love’ in one central group, producing pin-cushion flowerheads surrounded by papery bracts in soft pink, deep claret and stronger red-pink shades. Their branched wiry stems hold the flowers above lobed leaves from early into late summer. Unlike the drought-led Festuca and Delosperma nearby, Astrantia needs moisture-retentive soil to avoid scorched foliage and a shortened display.",
    months: ["Jun", "Jul", "Aug", "Sep"], size: "45–75cm", sizeDetail: "Cultivars differ; flowering stems rise above compact clumps", position: "Sun or light shade", positionDetail: "Light shade helps where soil dries quickly", soil: "Humus-rich and moisture-retentive", soilDetail: "Moist but drained, not baked dry", hardiness: "H6–H7", hardinessDetail: "All three are hardy garden cultivars", feature: "Three colours of pin-cushion flowers", featureDetail: "Papery bracts hold their structure after bloom", identity: "‘Buckland’, ‘Claret’ and ‘Star of Love’", identityDetail: "Three cultivar names retained as one planted group",
