    about: "Delosperma are southern African ice plants with fleshy leaves and daisy-family flowers that respond to strong light. Ice Cream Mix is a commercial colour mixture rather than one uniform botanical cultivar, so individual plants may vary in colour, vigour and cold survival. All share a need for sun and mineral drainage.", provenance: "The Ice Cream Mix label is retained, but the named components of the mixture are not documented.", family: "Aizoaceae", genus: "Delosperma", foliage: "Evergreen and succulent", habit: "Prostrate and mat-forming", botanicalLabel: "Name status", botanicalValue: "Commercial colour mix", role: "Low pastel succulent carpet in the sunny open ground", observation: "The mixed daisies supply late colour below the bed’s woody framework.", added: "Added July 2026", status: "Record which colours survive the first winter and improve grit around any failing crowns.", source: RHS.delosperma,
