    caution: "Leaves, stems and seed kernels are harmful if eaten. Wear gloves when handling and keep prunings away from pets, children and livestock.", about: "Prunus laurocerasus is a vigorous evergreen cherry relative from south-eastern Europe and western Asia. Its dense foliage makes excellent screening and shelter but can suppress smaller plants and become difficult to reduce if neglected. The species also has potential to become a nuisance, so fruit and self-sown seedlings should be monitored.", provenance: "The large glossy evergreen leaves and established boundary habit support Prunus laurocerasus at species level.", family: "Rosaceae", genus: "Prunus", foliage: "Evergreen, large and glossy", habit: "Dense, bushy and vigorous", role: "Permanent boundary screen and wildlife shelter", observation: "This is the strongest existing evergreen mass in Front Bed 5 and sets the scale for all newer plants.", status: "Maintain access and light with selective pruning, checking for nests before every major cut.", source: RHS.laurel,
