    under: "soft tips, small flowers or early leaf fall during sustained drought", over: "yellow foliage and weak growth while the root zone remains saturated", spring: "Feed and mulch after rain, then wait for the flowering pattern before making more than a light structural prune.", summer: "Deadhead selected blooms if repeat flowering is wanted, but leave some spent flowers to develop hips and photograph the full bloom.", autumn: "Retain sound hips for colour and birds, and clear leaves badly affected by black spot.", winter: "Remove dead, damaged and crossing stems, thinning rather than shortening every shoot until the rose class is known.",
    problem: { name: "Cultivar-blind pruning", sign: "A hard annual cut removes the wood that would have carried the next display", response: "Record whether flowers form on old or new growth and whether they repeat before adopting a class-specific pruning routine." },
