    description: "The established standard is bay, Laurus nobilis: leathery aromatic evergreen leaves held on a clipped head above a clear stem. It brings permanent height to Front Bed 5 and can supply culinary leaves when the plant is healthy and has not been sprayed. Bay tolerates clipping but responds best to selective late-spring or summer cuts, with the root zone kept drained and the crown protected from the harshest wind.",
